# -- end of source
# The pattern's own default `{}` has a layout that lists the four names; `tint` and `edge` are written nowhere, and nothing but the default makes such an object. It was the one layout that answers all the names,
# so it alone was expected of the argument, and the guess failed at every call that hands an object. Names that are never written tell no layout from another: the literal's layout, which answers the names that are
# written, is expected beside it, and the names that it lacks are found absent behind two looks at the cell.
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}} key="label"
# CHECK: = HasNoExtraProperties
# CHECK: = HasLayoutPrototype
# RUN(COUNT): compile LayoutsExpectedBesideOneWhoseOtherNamesAreNeverWritten mechanisms=all
# COUNT-NOT: LayoutsExpectedBesideOneWhoseOtherNamesAreNeverWritten 0
# COUNT: statistic LayoutsExpectedBesideOneWhoseOtherNamesAreNeverWritten
